{"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/collectorencoding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatch"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/SkippedRecord","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder"},{"text":" is the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BatchEncoder"},{"text":" for a self-hosted TraffluentCollector’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/v1\/batches"},{"text":". Give it to an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"text":") as its encoder,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and pass the collector’s API key to the destination as an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Authorization: Bearer"},{"text":" header field.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is JSON: one object per record, with the record’s identifier (which a redelivered record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps), the event’s name, its timestamp, whether it is redelivered, its properties and its context.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Properties are read from the event’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryCodable"},{"text":" form, which ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" derives, through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. The context holds the standard","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context keys the record has values for, its session and sample rate, and its trace context. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" value is written only while the record reveals it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one whose event and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"version the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryCodable"},{"type":"text","text":", and one holding a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"JSON can’t, such as a NaN. Each is logged; "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder\/batch(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns the body"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with each record left out as a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":". When no record of a batch can be written,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder\/encode(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" throws, and the destination sends nothing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to a server of your own format, write a ","type":"text"},{"code":"BatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of your own. To send to PostHog,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use ","type":"text"},{"code":"PostHogBatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import CollectorEncoding","import HTTPDestinations","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = TrackingPlan(schemas: [SignedUp.schema])","let encoder = CollectorBatchEncoder(plan: plan)","let collector = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: collectorURL,  \/\/ https:\/\/collector.example.com\/v1\/batches","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(apiKey)\"],","    encoder: encoder)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: collector)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers sending to the collector beside the other destinations.","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding"},"abstract":[{"text":"Write batches of records in TraffluentCollector’s ingest format, for an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to send.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework","title":"CollectorEncoding","externalID":"CollectorEncoding","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"CollectorEncoding"}]},"references":{"doc://CollectorEncoding/documentation/CollectorEncoding":{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write batches of records in TraffluentCollector’s ingest format, for an "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to send."}],"title":"CollectorEncodin